    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "Once I've used the shared calendar and weekly digest for a few weeks and confirmed they reduce my mental load, Plus makes sense. Pro's email parsing is nice but not essential—I'd upgrade to Plus first and evaluate Pro later.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_annual_after_long_use",
      "rationale": "I'm cautious about prepaying for apps. After two or three months of daily use proving the product sticks in our routine, I'd commit to annual billing for the discount.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 trial month is low risk and removes friction. I'd try Plus features at that price, but I'd cancel immediately if I don't see clear value—no guilt at a dollar.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm not against paying for the right tool, but I'd do a quick comparison first. If FocusLoop clearly beats the alternative for our family's workflow, I'd pay without hesitation.",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads on a family app would be mildly annoying, but I wouldn't pay just to remove them. I'd upgrade to Plus only if the digest, handoffs, and shared calendar justify the cost—ad-free is a bonus, not the reason.",
      "confidence": 0.81
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99/month for Plus, the pricing is reasonable for a tool that could save hours of coordination stress. But it only feels fair if we actually use it daily—I won't pay for potential.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
